Package: hexglobe
Title: Render 'hexify' Globes on the Graphics Card Without a Browser
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Draws the globes of the 'hexify' package offscreen on the
    graphics card through 'wgpu', the 'Rust' implementation of 'WebGPU',
    with the same shader and pipelines as the 'hexify' globe widget, and
    returns the image as pixels or a PNG file. 'hexify' calls it from
    hex_globe_png(); no browser is needed.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), hexify
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
